# paddleocr-vl-service is a fully separate deployable unit (its own
# Dockerfile/venv/uv.lock, `context: ./backend/paddleocr-vl-service` in
# docker-compose.yml) living inside backend/ purely for source-location
# convenience (SA1.2 folder-structure review, 2026-08-10) — it must never
# be copied into the backend-api/backend-worker/backend-worker-gpu build
# context. This also fixes a real build-context-size bug found during F4
# verification: without this line, `paddleocr-vl-service/.venv` (~7GB, a
# local dev venv, itself covered by the top `.venv/` rule already but
# nested one level deeper than expected) was being transferred into every
# backend/ image's build context.
paddleocr-vl-service/
